{"parentUuid":"e04d4044-2596-43d5-b411-0e221ef40e2f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgv3BWdmaBEaDXcDcWAbF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The tool pages and Caliper's two evidence pages now have a chapter list: numbered entries in the left rail with a \"Back to top\" link, and the content on the reading column beside it. The `orin-dx` format, typecheck, lint and test checks all exit 0. `orin-dx:build` built all 16 pages and `orin-dx:verify` reported \"16 pages checked, ok\" (dead links, anchors, alt text).\n\nI looked at the parity page at desktop and phone width, and the main Caliper page and Wisp at desktop width, in light theme only. I did not look at the other seven tool pages, the measurement page's final render or dark theme. The checks cover the other seven only through the build.\n\nThe mechanism: the evidence layout and the shared `[tool].astro` template now use the system's `DocumentPage`, the same one Principles uses. All nine tool pages (the template builds the chapter list from the same conditions that decide which sections exist) and Caliper's two sub-pages get it. The trail sits above the document as the breadcrumbs design doc requires. The hero is the document's lead, so `ToolHero` and `ToolPageHero` gained a `headingId`.\n\nDetails and caveats:\n- **Sections:** they are now `frame` width with a small spacing wrapper, as Principles does it, because `PageSection` doesn't space children in that mode. Section labels are plain words (such as \"the job\" and \"wrong types\"), because the rail numbers them.\n- **Phone width:** on the parity page the rail isn't visible in the viewport. I'd expect it to move into the menu as the system's chapter design does, but I did not open the menu to confirm.\n- **Side effect on tool pages:** the right-hand source notes now sit after each section's content instead of beside it. The Caliper main page shows the same arrangement. If you'd like them back in the rail, that needs a layout decision for document pages.\n- **The 'text' mistake:** I first tried `width=\"text\"` and the sections spilled across the rail, which is why the pages use `frame`.\n\nA backup of the original template is in the job's tmp folder. Nothing is committed. The pages repo has 19 changed or new files: the hero and table components, the lattice level, the shared data, the three Caliper pages, the template and two docs and stories.\n\nOpen items:\n- the kicker/slot refactor, still waiting on your yes;\n- the unused `ParityPlot`;\n- the Caliper-side change to score RDT on real components and list the props behind counts.\n\nShall I commit this on a branch in the pages repo?\n\nresult: Tool pages and Caliper's evidence pages now have the system's chapter list (all nine tools via the shared template), with `orin-dx` format, typecheck, lint, test, build (16 pages) and verify all passing, uncommitted in `~/projects/pages`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":639287,"output_tokens":916,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":916,"cache_read_input_tokens":639287,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"56f47498-b616-4ddc-81cd-0f5d5c7ab785","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgv3BWGhG3b1bPDcbSrod","requestRef":"f2170e1c-239d-431d-8075-ed61adbf3079","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e9e780a-9a55