{"parentUuid":"d5cda0da-d23f-47ce-a5ec-f10f38a42742","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"022ad259-3231-429f-b0ad-a7b57b031ee0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJGAJ7kTGtQatpXNHQLNz1","type":"tool_result","content":"packages/twx/dist/panda/preset.mjs\npackages/brand/techworx/project/tokens.json\npackages/brand/test/tokens.test.ts\npackages/brand/shared/scripts/README.md\npackages/brand/shared/scripts/stage_artifact.py\npackages/brand/techworx/project/tokens.json:3367:  \"roleZIndex\": {\npackages/brand/test/tokens.test.ts:79:    ['zIndex', 'roleZIndex'],\npackages/brand/shared/scripts/README.md:56:The source `tokens.json` files are complete and drive Panda; they are never changed by the stager. The artifact gets a fitted, derived copy (`fit_tokens` in `stage_artifact.py`) because the format caps families (12 with color and type), tokens per family (60) and allows aliases only in colour tokens. The fit resolves non-colour aliases to literals (shadows get each theme's resolved colours, kept per theme where they differ), merges `roleSpace` and `roleStep` into `spacing`, `roleRadius` into `radius` and `roleSize` into `size` (the overflow continues in `roleSize`), and renames `roleZIndex`, `roleBorderWidth` and `roleShadow` to `zIndex`, `borderWidth` and `shadow`. Dropped: the ten `roleStep` tokens, as duplicates of spacing tokens with the same values. Anything else the format cannot hold is listed under `notRepresented` in the staged `upload-manifest.json`, and the run prints a count. `--strict` refuses on any remaining cap breach. `test/artifactFit.test.ts` runs the stager for both brands and checks the caps and that every source token is present or listed.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"082b7ce7-3163-41bc-8696-8ff823ba2c46","timestamp":"2026-11-10T22:39:48.335Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"packages/twx/dist/panda/preset.mjs\npackages/brand/techworx/project/tokens.json\npackages/brand/test/tokens.test.ts\npackages/brand/shared/scripts/README.md\npackages/brand/shared/scripts/stage_artifact.py\npackages/brand/techworx/project/tokens.json:3367:  \"roleZIndex\": {\npackages/brand/test/tokens.test.ts:79:    ['zIndex', 'roleZIndex'],\npackages/brand/shared/scripts/README.md:56:The source `tokens.json` files are complete and drive Panda; they are never changed by the stager. The artifact gets a fitted, derived copy (`fit_tokens` in `stage_artifact.py`) because the format caps families (12 with color and type), tokens per family (60) and allows aliases only in colour tokens. The fit resolves non-colour aliases to literals (shadows get each theme's resolved colours, kept per theme where they differ), merges `roleSpace` and `roleStep` into `spacing`, `roleRadius` into `radius` and `roleSize` into `size` (the overflow continues in `roleSize`), and renames `roleZIndex`, `roleBorderWidth` and `roleShadow` to `zIndex`, `borderWidth` and `shadow`. Dropped: the ten `roleStep` tokens, as duplicates of spacing tokens with the same values. Anything else the format cannot hold is listed under `notRepresented` in the staged `upload-manifest.json`, and the run prints a count. `--strict` refuses on any remaining cap breach. `test/artifactFit.test.ts` runs the stager for both brands and checks the caps and that every source token is present or listed.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5c905547-6e1f-4669-9ce3-6d50746d9765","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":