{"parentUuid":"1a13dde1-fa3e-4f97-a110-60cfa668dfbe","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01T7tFStZAc4Yb17rNDWkR7w","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk git fetch -q origin main 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"=== caliper repo docs: stale framing/figures\\\"; git grep -n -i -E \\\"28×|0\\\\.38 s|recall against rdt|yardstick|99\\\\.7|parity\\\\.md|31×\\\" origin/main -- README.md STATUS.md docs/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -14; echo; echo \\\"=== caliper docs that mention the weekly-record scope caveats\\\"; git grep -n -i -E \\\"non-component|counted once for each|per-prop rows|scored on real components\\\" origin/main -- docs/measurement.md docs/rdt-differences.md | head -6\\ncd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && echo; echo \\\"=== docs site (orin-dx-docs) caliper content\\\"; grep -rli \\\"caliper\\\" apps/orin-dx-docs/src 2>/dev/null | head; echo; echo \\\"=== guidance docs mention of what we built\\\"; rtk grep -n -i -E \\\"shared scale|rowTones|groupSize|ComparisonBars|TypeBoundaries|chapter|DocumentPage|count with|share of\\\" docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md | head; echo; echo \\\"=== API reference for changed components\\\"; rtk grep -n -E \\\"groupSize|rowTones|toolField|headingId|zIndex.rail|zIndex.trail\\\" docs/design-system-api.md | head -5\",\"description\":\"Check where the lessons are and aren't recorded in docs\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":19},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6b705f49-3f4c-4d32-832f-04bf98825a56","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:50:01.937Z","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"1a13dde1-fa3e-4f97-a110-60cfa668dfbe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"911f03b1-a511-4bc4-afa6-255cd7ac70fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T7tFStZAc4Yb17rNDWkR7w","type":"tool_result","content":"=== caliper repo docs: stale framing/figures\norigin/main:docs/STATUS.md:16:- **Speed** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on the same files. No pull-request gate enforces it: a weekly workflow records speed, memory and recall against RDT and react-docgen and opens an issue on a worsening, and `just bench` compares a branch with `main` locally (`docs/measurement.md`).\norigin/main:docs/benchmarks.md:213:# Whole-library record: Caliper, RDT and react-docgen, with recall against RDT and the TS 7.1 oracle\norigin/main:docs/measurement.md:77:The run uploads `weekly.json` and a table to the job summary, which opens with a short \"how to read these numbers\" paragraph and the headline (below). It compares with the last successful run's `weekly.json` and opens, or comments on, one issue labelled `weekly-measurement` only for what is a problem on its own (see \"The headline\"): a wrong type above the gate or higher than last week, a silent-wrong answer to a reader's question, or a whole run over a budget. Drift in time, memory, recall against RDT and the agent correct rate is listed in the summary under \"Changes since last week\" and opens nothing: a shared CI machine moves by 10% or more on its own, and recall against RDT is how much of RDT's output we also report, not whether our types are right. There is no committed baseline: the previous run is the baseline for what rose.\norigin/main:docs/measurement.md:133:Recall against RDT stays information. A local run on antd and shadcn at the commit that added this, with the default collapse, reads: antd 83.7% correct, 6.0% less precise, 0.00% wrong, 10.2% named only (3,426 props); shadcn 54.4% correct, 5.1% less precise, 0.06% wrong (0.096% of the judged props, just under the gate), 0.4% missing, 39.6% named only (13,918 props). The weekly record collapses nothing (`--collapse-inherited-props none`), so named only is 0 there; its run of 2026-11-06 reads antd 94.0% correct, 6.0% less precise, 0 wrong, and shadcn 93.8% correct, 5.3% less precise, 8 wrong (0.058% of the shared props), 0.4% missing (`headline` in `weekly.json`, `main` at `c5fbb33e`). Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum read in that run: 90.9%, 100.0% and 83.7% agree, with 0, 1 and 22 wrong. Of Spectrum's 22, the comparator's index-signature artifact accounts for all (`docs/rdt-differences.md`), so that gate firing is false until the comparator is corrected.\norigin/main:docs/measurement.md:277:| mantine  |            331/389 |                    99.7% |    55 ms, 109 MiB |    1.3 s, 458 MiB |\norigin/main:docs/measurement.md:281:| spectrum |          1087/1408 |                    99.7% |   130 ms, 219 MiB |    2.2 s, 828 MiB |\norigin/main:docs/performance.md:120:Output is exact: the new default is byte-identical to the previous build's `--load-dependencies` output, and `--no-load-dependencies` to the previous default. Share of react-docgen-typescript's props reported, off → on (the 0.4.0 baseline, since removed): Chakra 0.1% → 98.6%, shadcn 6.4% → 39.5%, antd 71.8% → 80.3%, Mantine and Spectrum 99.7% both. The cost lands on a few projects: Chakra is 4.4× slower and holds 3.3× the memory, shadcn takes 40 ms and 124 MiB more, the others 10 to 20 ms and 16 to 25 MiB. A CI job that needs the old speed passes `--no-load-dependencies`.\norigin/main:docs/rdt-coverage.md:388:**Found by:** the Storybook parity report on antd (`packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs`, `docs/storybook-parity.md`), against Storybook's docgen.\n\n=== caliper docs that mention the weekly-record scope caveats\norigin/main:docs/rdt-differences.md:340:**Measured.** RDT's score against the checker is in the table (`oracle.tools.rdt`), by the same rules as Caliper's. The reference for recall removes the non-components and the repeats (`docs/measurement.md`).\n\n=== docs site (orin-dx-docs) caliper content\n\n=== guidance docs mention of what we built\n63:- Long tool documents should use the existing chapter rail from `DocumentPage`, with source notes beside the claims they support.\n\n=== API reference for changed components\n1352:| `./SectionHeading` | `./src/section-heading/sectionHeading.tsx` | component (`SectionHeading`: a section's opening, `label` 8 above a section-role heading with `headingId`; `after=\"content\"` (default, 24 to what follows) or `\"text\"` (16 to its own sentence)) |\n1551:| `headingId` | `string` | none | The `<h1>`'s id, so a region around the header (a document page's lead) can be named by it. |\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper\n<sandbox_violations>\ndeny network-outbound github.com:22 (not in this command's allowed_domains — re-run the command with this host listed if it needs it)\n</sandbox_violations>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d95064b8-491e-4276-a0cf-88d22a1c8cbb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:50:05.393Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== caliper repo docs: stale framing/figures\norigin/main:docs/STATUS.md:16:- **Speed** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on the same files. No pull-request gate enforces it: a weekly workflow records speed, memory and recall against RDT and react-docgen and opens an issue on a worsening, and `just bench` compares a branch with `main` locally (`docs/measurement.md`).\norigin/main:docs/benchmarks.md:213:# Whole-library record: Caliper, RDT and react-docgen, with recall against RDT and the TS 7.1 oracle\norigin/main:docs/measurement.md:77:The run uploads `weekly.json` and a table to the job 