{"parentUuid":"a6030143-5fe3-4ca9-ba3f-bd3a6bcdfcd8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"911f03b1-a511-4bc4-afa6-255cd7ac70fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AzkJq3wpPwRpAEnA6rGqqs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t- [Stacked PR retargeting](stacked-pr-retargeting.md) — retarget children to main when a parent merges, or GitHub closes them\n2\t- [Sandbox, git and gh](sandbox-git-and-gh.md) — gh and git commits need the sandbox off; one plain git command per call\n3\t- [Plan trails before branches](plan-trails-before-branches.md) — plan feature trails and assign branches first; PRs only via the gh shim, then link at once\n4\t- [Storybook is the goal](storybook-is-the-goal.md) — Storybook integration is the product's purpose; roadmap's \"out of scope\" is stale\n5\t- [TS 7.1 backend is experimental opt-in](ts71-backend-experimental-opt-in.md) — off by default; `auto` later needs oracle evidence and a new ADR\n6\t- [Entire trails: no tables](entire-trails-no-tables.md) — trail bodies don't render MD tables; use bullets\n7\t- [Push sessions before worktree exit](push-sessions-before-worktree-exit.md) — commit + push the branch and check `entire checkpoint list --outgoing` before removing a worktree\n8\t- [Type correctness over RDT parity](type-correctness-over-rdt-parity.md) — judge by correct types in Storybook (layers fine); first load imperceptible; RDT recall is only information\n9\t- [Measurement must match the real consumer](measurement-must-match-real-consumer.md) — use the addon's real config (collapse 'none'); verify worker numbers before stating them\n10\t- [Measure memory and time](measure-memory-and-time.md) — check Chakra+deps peak RSS, not only wall time, for resolver changes\n11\t- [Workers run the full lint gate](workers-run-full-lint-gate.md) — require `just lint doc-check machete typos` before push; verify CI before saying done\n12\t- [Schedule overlapping work sequentially](schedule-overlapping-work-sequentially.md) — conflicts are my scheduling fault; one PR at a time on shared files, stop rule, read gates not just checks\n13\t- [Run the oracle sparingly](run-the-oracle-sparingly.md) — oracle and corpus runs cost real money; only when asked or once per merged batch, never to confirm a PR\n14\t- [Checker-first plan and workflow](checker-first-plan-and-workflow.md) — ADR 0026 / trail 259 slices S1-S8, stacking and merge-commit rules, worktree and orchestration lessons\n15\t- [No durable state in /tmp](no-durable-state-in-tmp.md) — worker rules, inputs, harnesses go in the repo or memory, never /tmp (wiped on restart)\n16\t- [Trail comments refused for agents](trail-comments-refused-for-agents.md) — `entire trail comment add` is blocked from Claude sessions; use PR bodies, docs, findings\n17\t- [Workers do not poll CI](workers-do-not-poll-ci.md) — workers push and stop; the lead watches CI once; \"Entire Gates pending\" = awaiting the user\n18\t"}]},"uuid":"95a63bc4-6068-4862-a741-eba8f6e0b6b5","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:50:24.241Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/MEMORY.md","content":"- [Stacked PR retargeting](stacked-pr-retargeting.md) — retarget children to main when a parent merges, or GitHub closes them\n- [Sandbox, git and gh](sandbox-git-and-gh.md) — gh and git commits need the sandbox off; one plain git command per call\n- [Plan trails before branches](plan-trails-before-branches.md) — plan feature trails and assign branches first; PRs only via the gh shim, then link at once\n- [Storybook is the goal](storybook-is-the-goal.md) — Storybook integration is the product's purpose; roadmap's \"out of scope\" is stale\n- [TS 7.1 backend is experimental opt-in](ts71-backend-experimental-opt-in.md) — off by default; `auto` later needs oracle evidence and a new ADR\n- [Entire trails: no tables](entire-trails-no-tables.md) — trail bodies don't render MD tables; use bullets\n- [Push sessions before worktree exit](push-sessions-before-worktree-exit.md) — commit + push the branch and check `entire checkpoint list --outgoing` before removing a worktree\n- [Type correctness over RDT parity](type-correctness-over-rdt-parity.md) — judge by correct types in Storybook (layers fine); first load imperceptible; RDT recall is only information\n- [Measurement must match the real consumer](measurement-must-match-real-consumer.md) — use the addon's real config (collapse 'none'); verify worker numbers before stating them\n- [Measure memory and time](measure-memory-and-time.md) — check Chakra+deps peak RSS, not only wall time, for resolver changes\n- [Workers run the full lint gate](workers-run-full-lint-gate.md) — require `just lint doc-check machete typos` before push; verify CI before saying done\n- [Schedule overlapping work sequentially](schedule-overlapping-work-sequentially.md) — conflicts are my scheduling fault; one PR at a time on shared files, stop rule, read gates not just checks\n- [Run the oracle sparingly](run-the-oracle-sparingly.md) — oracle and corpus runs cost real money; only when asked or once per merged batch, never to confirm a PR\n- [Checker-first plan and workflow](checker-first-plan-and-workflow.md) — ADR 0026 / trail 259 slices S1-S8, stacking and merge-commit rules, worktree and orchestration lessons\n- [No durable state in /tmp](no-durable-state-in-tmp.md) — worker rules, inputs, harnesses go in the repo or memory, never /tmp (wiped on restart)\n- [Trail comments refused for agents](trail-comments-refused-for-agents.md) — `entire trail comment add` is blocked from Claude sessions; use PR bodies, docs, findings\n- [Workers do not poll CI](workers-do-not-poll-ci.md) — workers push and stop; the lead watches CI once; \"Entire Gates pending\" = awaiting the user\n","numLines":18,"startLine":1,"totalLines":18}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a6030143-5fe3-4ca9-ba3f-bd3a6bcdfcd8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
