{"parentUuid":"b1d225a8-0ef8-4635-b2f5-744d76b51191","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9b55362c-3f93-4b33-9ee2-e65c2097841d","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:50:24.261Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","hash":"47166680ba8722698786f7e28f630cfdab60903af267fab1786ec153fd13f547","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Checking against the current `origin/main` docs, the answer is no. Here is where the lessons stand, and I'm also saving the main working-style correction to memory."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UHLgSABvStR3CbqBjHBNqP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/use-existing-components-and-tokens.md","content":"---\nname: use-existing-components-and-tokens\ndescription: On the Orin DX pages repo, find and reuse the system's component, recipe or token before building anything; read the layout and opener rules first\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nOn `~/projects/pages` (orin-dx site, `packages/orin`, `packages/foundations`): look for the existing component, recipe, slot or token first, and read the system's own rules before composing a layout.\n\n**Why:** across the evidence-page work I repeatedly invented things (a hand-built hero header, local card styles in a 2×2 grid, ad-hoc `lx-page` classes, a bare lattice with no star, a borrowed `toggle.raised` z-index) and the user rejected each one (\"WTF are you inventing new things\", \"use what we have\"). The fix each time was an existing piece: `ToolHero` and `DocumentPage` for openers and the chapter list, `TypeBoundaries` for code plus result, `ComparisonBars` for charts, `ItemGroups`, and role tokens in `packages/brand/*/project/tokens.json`.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Before building: grep `packages/orin/src`, `apps/orin-dx/src/components`, and the opener/layout docs (`docs/plans/page-layouts.md`, `packages/orin/src/opener/openerAnatomy.ts`, `docs/design-system-rules.md`: composition over configuration).\n- Prefer composition (slots, ReactNode props) to enum or boolean config flags; add an optional data prop to an existing component only when composition is impossible (`.astro` cannot pass styled React nodes).\n- Layers get semantic role tokens in both brands' tokens.json (`zIndex.popup`, `.overlay`, `.rail`, `.trail`), never literals or another component's token.\n- Verify with Playwright screenshots (desktop and phone) and run `orin-dx` format, typecheck, lint, test, build and verify; moon needs the sandbox off.\n- Judge numbers by correctness against the checker and state the counting unit, denominators and scope of each tool before presenting a comparison; see [[type-correctness-over-rdt-parity]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AzkJq3wpPwRpAEnA6rGqqs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/MEMORY.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","hash":"4f18ea624ec4eb6e147294ede1b6bcf4b1cedad7f87059be023660c2b6a176fd","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UHLgSABvStR3CbqBjHBNqP","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/use-existing-components-and-tokens.md"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AzkJq3wpPwRpAEnA6rGqqs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t- [Stacked PR retargeting](stacked-pr-retargeting.md) — retarget children to main when a parent merges, or GitHub closes them\n2\t- [Sandbox, git and gh](sandbox-git-and-gh.md) — gh and git commits need the sandbox off; one plain git command per call\n3\t- [Plan trails before branches](plan-trails-before-branches.md) — plan feature trails and assign branches first; PRs only via the gh shim, then link at once\n4\t- [Storybook is the goal](storybook-is-the-goal.md) — Storybook integration is the product's purpose; roadmap's \"out of scope\" is stale\n5\t- [TS 7.1 backend is experimental opt-in](ts71-backend-experimental-opt-in.md) — off by default; `auto` later needs oracle evidence and a new ADR\n6\t- [Entire trails: no tables](entire-trails-no-tables.md) — trail bodies don't render MD tables; use bullets\n7\t- [Push sessions before worktree exit](push-sessions-before-worktree-exit.md) — commit + push the branch and check `entire checkpoint list --outgoing` before removing a worktree\n8\t- [Type correctness over RDT parity](type-correctness-over-rdt-parity.md) — judge by correct types in Storybook (layers fine); first load imperceptible; RDT recall is only information\n9\t- [Measurement must match the real consumer](measurement-must-match-real-consumer.md) — use the addon's real config (collapse 'none'); verify worker numbers before stating them\n10\t- [Measure memory and time](measure-memory-and-time.md) — check Chakra+deps peak RSS, not only wall time, for resolver changes\n11\t- [Workers run the full lint gate](workers-run-full-lint-gate.md) — require `just lint doc-check machete typos` before push; verify CI before saying done\n12\t- [Schedule overlapping work sequentially](schedule-overlapping-work-sequentially.md) — conflicts are my scheduling fault; one PR at a time on shared files, stop rule, read gates not just checks\n13\t- [Run the oracle sparingly](run-the-oracle-sparingly.md) — oracle and corpus runs cost real money; only when asked or once per merged batch, never to confirm a PR\n14\t- [Checker-first plan and workflow](checker-first-plan-and-workflow.md) — ADR 0026 / trail 259 slices S1-S8, stacking and merge-commit rules, worktree and orchestration lessons\n15\t- [No durable state in /tmp](no-durable-state-in-tmp.md) — worker rules, inputs, harnesses go in the repo or memory, never /tmp (wiped on restart)\n16\t- [Trail comments refused for agents](trail-comments-refused-for-agents.md) — `entire trail comment add` is blocked from Claude sessions; use PR bodies, docs, findings\n17\t- [Workers do not poll CI](workers-do-not-poll-ci.md) — workers push and stop; the lead watches CI once; \"Entire Gates pending\" = awaiting the user\n18\t"}]}}
