{"parentUuid":"4bc8515a-672b-4c3d-acf7-db9601e5604b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Vyu7U6YnMZT2NXD1aN3WpP","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3c98e64e-c0ee-4d88-9be4-fb01dadea2b0","timestamp":"2026-11-11T04:50:36.485Z","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"3c98e64e-c0ee-4d88-9be4-fb01dadea2b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvYCQXZXQYSxnfWZxUeU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, we haven't applied them to the docs. The pages now carry the new story, and the docs around them still tell the old one. I checked three places.\n\n**1. The Caliper repo docs are stale or contradict the pages**\n- **`docs/STATUS.md`** still says \"17 to 39 times faster, 34 to 81 ms\", the October laptop run. The current record is 16 to 66× faster and 2.5 to 5.8× less memory on CI, and memory ratios aren't stated anywhere.\n- **`docs/measurement.md`:**\n  - It still tabulates the October 0.4.0 numbers with \"99.7%\", the RDT-as-yardstick framing we moved away from. It says Spectrum's gate firing is \"false until the comparator is corrected\", but the November 9 record shows 0 wrong there.\n  - It has none of the caveats we found: counts are (component × prop) occurrences, RDT is scored on every function it lists including non-components, and Caliper's less-precise share is higher than RDT's on three of five libraries.\n- **`docs/rdt-differences.md`** is the November 6 table. **`docs/performance.md`** still quotes the 99.7% shares.\n- **A docs-site gap:** `apps/orin-dx-docs` has no Caliper pages at all. If \"the docs\" means that site, there's nothing to update yet.\n\n**2. The pages-repo docs don't record what we built**\n- `docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md` should hold the recipe for an evidence page, and it doesn't:\n  - claim, then charts, then counts, then limits;\n  - counts shown with their share and denominator;\n  - one scale for like units;\n  - paired rows with role colours;\n  - examples via `TypeBoundaries`;\n  - one dated data module feeding every page.\n- The API reference doesn't list the new props: `Table`'s `groupSize` and `rowTones`, `ComparisonBars`'s `scale`, the `ToolHero` props and the `toolField` lattice level. `TypeBoundaries`' optional state also isn't listed. Nor does it explain the `rail` and `trail` tokens or the trail-before-wrapper rule.\n- I added Storybook stories for `ToolHero` only, none for `Table`, `ComparisonBars` or `TypeBoundaries`.\n\n**3. Still open**\n- The hero kicker and slots refactor, which I said I'd do as composition per your rules.\n- Scoring RDT on real components and listing the props behind each count.\n\nI saved the working-style correction to memory: find the existing component or token first and prefer composition.\n\nMy recommendation, in order: first the pages-repo docs, which I can do right now and which sit beside the work. Then a Caliper docs-fix trail (needs a worktree and a PR, and the trail has to be planned before the branch). The pages-repo docs first would fix `tool-evidence-language.md`, the API reference and the stories. Shall I start there?\n\nresult: The docs have not caught up: the Caliper repo docs still carry October figures and miss the scope caveats, the pages-repo docs don't record the new patterns, and the docs site has no Caliper content. I propose pages-repo docs first, then a Caliper docs-fix trail, and no docs changes made yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":429,"cache_read_input_tokens":703208,"output_tokens":1072,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":429,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1072,"cache_read_input_tokens":703208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":429},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d9ae48