{"parentUuid":"ae29477f-09e6-4c94-9f14-45f1d1fd216b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Q23WnxU6sBskZW9H6zPuR5","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && rtk wc -l docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md; rtk read docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md; echo ======API-HEAD; rtk read docs/design-system-api.md --head-lines 12; rtk grep -n \\\"generated\\\\|Generated\\\" docs/design-system-api.md | head -3; rtk grep -rn \\\"design-system-api\\\" package.json scripts 2>/dev/null | head -3\",\"description\":\"Read the evidence-language guide and the API reference header\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":17},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4c4c940e-892a-4896-b002-d60ab91813a6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:52:34.752Z","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"ae29477f-09e6-4c94-9f14-45f1d1fd216b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"59b8b9da-3745-4467-ad83-b44577dbb5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n67\n# Evidence and documentation language\n\nStatus: proposal for review. This records the visual and component direction for Orin DX tool pages; it does not approve token changes.\n\n## The jobs\n\nA product page makes one promise, shows one concrete result, gives a measured reason to believe it, then links to the details. A documentation page lets an engineer inspect the input, output, method, version and limits without decoding decorative color.\n\nThe current roles cover page surfaces, family identity, type, status and one measurement accent. They do not yet say how to color multiple data series or distinguish a measured result from an estimate. Orin's `surface.sunken` also resolves to the same color as `surface`, so it cannot by itself create a distinct source pane.\n\nCode has its own seven semantic roles in the Orin Panda theme: keyword, literal, type, callable, scalar, parameter and comment. They reference brass, verdigris, lilac, sky, rose, lime and muted ink respectively. They describe syntax, not tool family or pass/fail status. Light code uses deeper inks that reach at least 6.8:1 on the pale code pane; dark code uses the brighter brand partners on Case. Plain text remains body ink. Punctuation stays muted, and the grammar's token classes decide where each role appears. The Button source specimen uses the same highlighter as the setup examples.\n\nAcross tool pages, the problem and answer stack on one reading line. Short, reviewed feature groups can use numbered editorial rows; longer lists keep cards so they remain scannable. Raw agent-visible output remains plain text so the specimen shows the bytes an agent receives; source code and commands use syntax colors. Long raw-output lines wrap visually inside their frame without changing the sample text.\n\n## Color by meaning\n\n| Job | Proposed roles | Rule |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| One comparison | `data.focus`, `data.reference`, `data.track`, `data.rule` | The subject gets one emphasis; every value is labeled. The track is scaffolding, never a data series. |\n| Multiple categories | `data.series.1` to `.5` | A curated order, stable within one figure and legend. Use a gap or keyline where neighboring colors touch. Do not borrow family colors as family labels. |\n| Magnitude | `data.sequential.1` to `.5` | One ordered lightness ramp. More color means more of the named quantity in both themes. |\n| Change around zero | `data.diverging.low`, `.mid`, `.high` | Two directions from a neutral midpoint. State the direction in text and show a zero rule. |\n| Outcome | Existing `status.pass`, `.warn`, `.fail` | Reserve for actual outcomes, with a word and icon. A fast result is not a “pass” by color alone. |\n| Metrics | Existing `text.measure` | Value first, then what it measures, then method/version/date in muted type. No colored number without its unit and scope. |\n| Evidence surfaces | `surface.evidence`, `surface.source`, `surface.output` | Name the jobs before adding new colors. Start as aliases to existing `surface`, `surface.sunken` and `bg.canvas`; add a primitive only if the paired panes still merge in both themes. |\n\nThe first single-comparison mapping can alias `data.focus` to `text.measure`, `data.reference` to `text.muted`, `data.track` to `surface.raised`, and `data.rule` to `border.control`. The five-category scale needs a curated light/dark sequence from the existing hue ramps, then chart-specific values if family associations or adjacent-color checks make those unsuitable. The semantic aliases keep chart choices out of page code.\n\nIn the current Caliper figures, brass means “read this series first.” It marks Caliper in the three-tool race and “after” in the request comparison; it does not mean success or identify the build family. The tool name and before/after labels make those subjects explicit. Rose identifies the build family in product navigation and artwork, not a bar's outcome. Green is reserved for a labeled status such as pass; a shorter time or higher parity is described in words, not declared good by hue. Parity's props found and same-control values are peer measures, so they share one data color and keep their direct labels. Do not assign a new color just to make a second bar different.\n\nAn initial five-series sequence, for figures that truly need five categories:\n\n| Series | Orin light | Orin dark | Source primitive |\n| ------ | ---------- | --------- | ---------------- |\n| 1      | `#2c779e`  | `#6bc4eb` | sky 700 / 400    |\n| 2      | `#b63c62`  | `#ed9cb1` | rose 700 / 400   |\n| 3      | `#597c19`  | `#9bca44` | lime 700 / 400   |\n| 4      | `#744ed7`  | `#bea9f3` | lilac 700 / 400  |\n| 5      | `#22695f`  | `#99e1d9` | verdigris        |\n\nEach candidate exceeds 4:1 against the current Orin `surface` in light mode and 8:1 in dark mode. Those figures establish visibility against the panel, not separation between touching series. The visual review should test the ordered sequence with realistic bars, lines and legends, including color vision simulation. Use as many series as the data needs; five is a ceiling for this first pass, not a target.\n\nTest meaningful bars, points, rules and neighboring regions against their adjacent colors at 3:1. Text stays at 4.5:1. Labels, shape, ordering and direct values carry the meaning when color is unavailable. Check both Orin themes and both techworx modes before promoting shared roles. [Carbon's palette guidance](https://www.carbondesignsystem.com/building-blocks/data-visualization/color-palettes) distinguishes categorical, sequential, diverging and alert palettes; [WCAG 2.2](https://www.w3.org/TR/wcag/) supplies the contrast and non-color requirements.\n\n## Component grammar\n\n| Pattern | Content | Recipe contract |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `EvidenceFigure` | Title, direct labels, unit, method, version/date, source link and caveat | `sva` slots for frame, plot, caption and method; `cva` for a small set of `kind` variants such as comparison, category and change. |\n| `Metric` | Value, label, scope and provenance | `sva` slots keep the lower text aligned across a set. A `state` variant says measured, preliminary estimate or source experiment in words; it does not change only color. |\n| `SourceOutput` | Real input beside actual generated output | `sva` slots for source, output and caption. Equal treatment for peer fields. A `selected` variant exists only for an actual interactive selection. |\n| `DocumentLink` | A title, a useful preview and an affordance | `sva` slots for body and footer; a `cva` variant may express hover/selected behavior. No strand edge. |\n| `EvidenceNote` | A nearby source, caveat or definition | Use the existing icon-led margin-note recipe and label the note's job. |\n| `ReleaseNotice` | What ships now, what is in source and what is experimental | Text and version do the work; tone variants are for genuine warning or availability states. |\n\nUse `sva` when parts of one component need coordinated styling and `cva` for a single element with meaningful variants. Put reusable recipes beside their components, and promote them to foundations only when two pages or brands need the same contract. Page-level `css()` remains appropriate for a one-off layout arrangement; it should not encode chart color or repeat the anatomy of a component.\n\n## Decoration and rhythm\n\n- Family color and tint identify a tool or family. They do not stand in for data status or a selected row.\n- The strand edge belongs to a primary product answer or a real brand illustration. Charts, document links, source panes and ordinary cards rely on typography and alignment.\n- A document moves from summary to figure to method to reference. One focal point per screen; the dense material comes later.\n- Long tool documents should use the existing chapter rail from `DocumentPage`, with source notes beside the claims they support.\n\n## First application\n\nCaliper's cold-run and addon-request charts now use slot recipes with focus/reference fill variants. The parity chart directly labels its two measures and uses one brass data fill; its Button fixture uses a source/output slot recipe with peer prop rows. The parity and measurement pages share note/explanation spacing through a small recipe. Callisto, Michi, Monokl and Wisp use the same source-note and code treatments, with numbered feature rows only where the copy is short enough to scan. Longer pages keep their card groups. The five-series sequence remains a proposal to test in both themes before updating the brand library source and generated semantic tokens together.\n(eval):1: =====API-HEAD not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q23WnxU6sBskZW9H6zPuR5"}]},"uuid":"69e34f90-346f-44b1-966c-9a3dcef95315","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:52:38.490Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n67\n# Evidence and documentation language\n\nStatus: proposal for review. This records the visual and component direction for Orin DX tool pages; it does not approve token changes.\n\n## The jobs\n\nA product page makes one promise, shows one concrete result, gives a measured reason to believe it, then links to the details. A documentation page lets an engineer inspect the input, output, method, version and limits without decoding decorative color.\n\nThe current roles cover page surfaces, family identity, type, status and one measurement accent. They do not yet say how to color multiple data series or distinguish a measured result from an estimate. Orin's `surface.sunken` also resolves to the same color as `surface`, so it cannot by itself create a distinct source pane.\n\nCode has its own seven semantic roles in the Orin Panda theme: keyword, literal, type, callable, scalar, parameter and comment. They reference brass, verdigris, lilac