Name the jobs before adding new colors. Start as aliases to existing `surface`, `surface.sunken` and `bg.canvas`; add a primitive only if the paired panes still merge in both themes. |\n\nThe first single-comparison mapping can alias `data.focus` to `text.measure`, `data.reference` to `text.muted`, `data.track` to `surface.raised`, and `data.rule` to `border.control`. The five-category scale needs a curated light/dark sequence from the existing hue ramps, then chart-specific values if family associations or adjacent-color checks make those unsuitable. The semantic aliases keep chart choices out of page code.\n\nIn the current Caliper figures, brass means “read this series first.” It marks Caliper in the three-tool race and “after” in the request comparison; it does not mean success or identify the build family. The tool name and before/after labels make those subjects explicit. Rose identifies the build family in product navigation and artwork, not a bar's outcome. Green is reserved for a labeled status such as pass; a shorter time or higher parity is described in words, not declared good by hue. Parity's props found and same-control values are peer measures, so they share one data color and keep their direct labels. Do not assign a new color just to make a second bar different.\n\nAn initial five-series sequence, for figures that truly need five categories:\n\n| Series | Orin light | Orin dark | Source primitive |\n| ------ | ---------- | --------- | ---------------- |\n| 1      | `#2c779e`  | `#6bc4eb` | sky 700 / 400    |\n| 2      | `#b63c62`  | `#ed9cb1` | rose 700 / 400   |\n| 3      | `#597c19`  | `#9bca44` | lime 700 / 400   |\n| 4      | `#744ed7`  | `#bea9f3` | lilac 700 / 400  |\n| 5      | `#22695f`  | `#99e1d9` | verdigris        |\n\nEach candidate exceeds 4:1 against the current Orin `surface` in light mode and 8:1 in dark mode. Those figures establish visibility against the panel, not separation between touching series. The visual review should test 