{"parentUuid":"991361c6-4320-420a-b8bb-43e5ffa13b7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZskT5tRafBkKorApY3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Updating the pages docs now: the API reference first (Lattice, ToolHero, a new Table section), then the evidence guide."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":713293,"output_tokens":2532,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2532,"cache_read_input_tokens":713293,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"025ff3e1-60b5-499a-81a7-a97589d02a1f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwZsk2HUKgY8whYavUxY","requestRef":"0560dd89-e432-4703-8c7f-e900864da789","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b99d6f2-c3f1-43c2-8c3a-ab4abf021815","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:53:05.929Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"1b99d6f2-c3f1-43c2-8c3a-ab4abf021815","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZskT5tRafBkKorApY3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UCtghzpd8LAhjyX6Z6UpbV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\npath = 'docs/design-system-api.md'\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\ndef replace_once(old, new):\n    global text\n    assert text.count(old) == 1, (text.count(old), old[:60])\n    text = text.replace(old, new)\n\n# Lattice: the `level` prop and its levels.\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `full` | `boolean` | none | Removes the radial fade mask so the hexagons cover the whole box. |\n| `soft` | `boolean` | none |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `level` | `'page' \\\\| 'home' \\\\| 'ignite' \\\\| 'tool' \\\\| 'toolField'` | none | How strong the field and its glow are. `page`: every page but the landing page, at 70% of its strength. `home`: the landing page and the brand page, full strength. `ignite`: the brand opener, where the glow rises and the field spreads once on load. `tool`: a tool page's field in its family colour with a broad haze behind the mark. `toolField`: the same field and depth with no haze, for an opener whose art is not a mark (strands, or nothing). |\n| `full` | `boolean` | none | Removes the radial fade mask so the hexagons cover the whole box. |\n| `soft` | `boolean` | none |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| Variant | Values | Default |\n| ------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `full`  | `true` | none    |\n\n**Attributes emitted**\n\n| Attribute     | Value                                           | Element |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Variant | Values | Default |\n| ------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `level` | `page`, `home`, `ignite`, `tool`, `toolField` | none |\n| `full`  | `true` | none    |\n\n**Attributes emitted**\n\n| Attribute     | Value                                           | Element |\"\"\")\n\n# ToolHero: art, meta, headingId; the lattice is always in the family colour.\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"- What it renders: a `<section aria-label={name}>` with a tinted lattice, a hero mark, a family chip, a heading, a `{ orin dx }` byline, a description, a stage and optional actions.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- What it renders: a `<section aria-label={name}>` with a lattice that is always in the tool's family colour, optional art (the tool's mark with its haze, or strands), a family chip, a heading, a `{ orin dx }` byline, a description, a stage and optional actions.\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `tool` | `ToolName` | required | Selects the default mark. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `tool` | `ToolName` | required | Selects the default mark. |\n| `art` | `'mark' \\\\| 'strands' \\\\| 'none'` | `'mark'` | What stands beside the text. `mark`: the tool's mark (or `mark`) over the family haze (`Lattice level=\"tool\"`). `strands`: the ribbon over its lit cells, in the family colour. `none`: the lattice alone, with no haze (`level=\"toolField\"`), for a page under the tool's own, which has no star of its own. |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `mark` | `ReactNode` | `<ToolMark tool={tool} size=\"fluid\" treatment=\"hero\" />` | Replaces the default mark. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `mark` | `ReactNode` | `<ToolMark tool={tool} size=\"fluid\" treatment=\"hero\" />` | Replaces the default mark when `art` is `mark`. |\n| `meta` | `boolean` | `true` | The family and stage chips under the description. A page under the tool's own leaves them off. |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `headingAs` | `'h1' \\\\| 'h2'` | `'h1'` | Heading element. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `headingAs` | `'h1' \\\\| 'h2'` | `'h1'` | Heading element. |\n| `headingId` | `string` | none | The title's id, so a region around the opener (a document page's lead) can be named by it. |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `data-family` | the family                                       | root                    |\n| `data-slot`   | slot name                                        | each slot element       |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `data-family` | the family                                       | root                    |\n| `data-art`    | `mark`, `strands` or `none`                      | root                    |\n| `data-slot`   | slot name                                        | each slot element       |\"\"\")\n\n# Table: it is in the exports map but had no section.\ntable = \"\"\"#### Table\n\n- Import: `import { Table } from '@pages/orin/Table'` (also exports type `TableProps`)\n- Source: `packages/orin/src/table/table.tsx`; recipe: `tableRecipe` in `packages/orin/src/table/tableRecipe.ts`.\n- Tests: `packages/orin/src/table/table.test.tsx`.\n- What it renders: a keyboard-focusable scroll region named by the caption, holding a `<table>` with a mono column-label row. The first cell of each row is its row header.\n- Usage: in use. Consumers in apps: orin-dx: tool pages, the Caliper evidence pages.\n\n**Props**\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `caption` | `string` | required | Names the scroll region and the table. |\n| `hideCaption` | `boolean` | `false` | Keeps the caption for assistive technology and does not draw it, when a heading above names the table. |\n| `columns` | `readonly string[]` | required | The column labels. Keep each to one short word where you can: a heading that repeats a tool's name across columns reads badly. Put the tool in a column instead (one row per tool). |\n| `rows` | `readonly (readonly ReactNode[])[]` | required | One array of cells per row. |\n| `groupSize` | `number` | none | Rows that belong together, such as a Caliper row and its RDT row: a heavier rule closes each group. |\n| `rowTones` | `readonly ('focus' \\\\| 'reference' \\\\| undefined)[]` | none | The role of each row by index, in the colours the charts use: `focus` is the subject in `text.measure`, `reference` is what it is held against in `text.muted`. |\n| `classes` | `{ root?, table?, caption?, head?, cell? }` (strings) | none | Appended per slot by `mergeSlots`. |\n| `...rest` | `ComponentPropsWithRef<'div'>` minus `children`, `className` | none | Spread onto the root `<div>`. |\n\n**Attributes emitted**: `data-recipe=\"table\"` on the root, `data-slot` on each part, `data-group-end` on every cell of the last row of a group, `data-tone` on every cell of a toned row.\n\n**Accessibility**:\n\n- The root is `role=\"region\"` with `aria-label` equal to the caption and `tabIndex={0}`, so a table wider than its column scrolls by keyboard.\n- Colour is never the only carrier: a toned row also names its tool in a cell, and the values are always written out.\n\n\"\"\"\nreplace_once(\"#### PageSection\\n\", table + \"#### PageSection\\n\")\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(text)\nprint('api reference updated')\nEOF","description":"Update the API reference for Lattice, ToolHero and Table"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":713293,"output_tokens":2532,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2532,"cache_read_input_tokens":713293,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1166},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UCtghzpd8LAhjyX6Z6UpbV":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\npath = 'docs/design-system-api.md'\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\ndef replace_once(old, new):\n    global text\n    assert text.count(old) == 1, (text.count(old), old[:60])\n    text = text.replace(old, new)\n\n# Lattice: the `level` prop and its levels.\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `full` | `boolean` | none | Removes the radial fade mask so the hexagons cover the whole box. |\n| `soft` | `boolean` | none |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `level` | `'page' \\\\| 'home' \\\\| 'ignite' \\\\| 'tool' \\\\| 'toolField'` | none | How strong the field and its glow are. `page`: every page but the landing page, at 70% of its strength. `home`: the landing page and the brand page, full strength. `ignite`: the brand opener, where the glow rises and the field spreads once on load. `tool`: a tool page's field in its family colour with a broad haze behind the mark. `toolField`: the same field and depth with no haze, for an opener whose art is not a mark (strands, or nothing). |\n| `full` | `boolean` | none | Removes the radial fade mask so the hexagons cover the whole box. |\n| `soft` | `boolean` | none |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| Variant | Values | Default |\n| ------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `full`  | `true` | none    |\n\n**Attributes emitted**\n\n| Attribute     | Value                                           | Element |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| Variant | Values | Default |\n| ------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `level` | `page`, `home`, `ignite`, `tool`, `toolField` | none |\n| `full`  | `true` | none    |\n\n**Attributes emitted**\n\n| Attribute     | Value                                           | Element |\"\"\")\n\n# ToolHero: art, meta, headingId; the lattice is always in the family colour.\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"- What it renders: a `<section aria-label={name}>` with a tinted lattice, a hero mark, a family chip, a heading, a `{ orin dx }` byline, a description, a stage and optional actions.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- What it renders: a `<section aria-label={name}>` with a lattice that is always in the tool's family colour, optional art (the tool's mark with its haze, or strands), a family chip, a heading, a `{ orin dx }` byline, a description, a stage and optional actions.\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `tool` | `ToolName` | required | Selects the default mark. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `tool` | `ToolName` | required | Selects the default mark. |\n| `art` | `'mark' \\\\| 'strands' \\\\| 'none'` | `'mark'` | What stands beside the text. `mark`: the tool's mark (or `mark`) over the family haze (`Lattice level=\"tool\"`). `strands`: the ribbon over its lit cells, in the family colour. `none`: the lattice alone, with no haze (`level=\"toolField\"`), for a page under the tool's own, which has no star of its own. |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `mark` | `ReactNode` | `<ToolMark tool={tool} size=\"fluid\" treatment=\"hero\" />` | Replaces the default mark. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `mark` | `ReactNode` | `<ToolMark tool={tool} size=\"fluid\" treatment=\"hero\" />` | Replaces the default mark when `art` is `mark`. |\n| `meta` | `boolean` | `true` | The family and stage chips under the description. A page under the tool's own leaves them off. |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `headingAs` | `'h1' \\\\| 'h2'` | `'h1'` | Heading element. |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `headingAs` | `'h1' \\\\| 'h2'` | `'h1'` | Heading element. |\n| `headingId` | `string` | none | The title's id, so a region around the opener (a document page's lead) can be named by it. |\"\"\")\nreplace_once(\n\"\"\"| `data-family` | the family                                       | root                    |\n| `data-slot`   | slot name                                        | each slot element       |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `data-family` | the family                                       | root                    |\n| `data-art`    | `mark`, `strands` or `none`                      | root                    |\n| `data-slot`   | slot name                                        | each slot element       |\"\"\")\n\n# Table: it is in the exports map but had no section.\ntable = \"\"\"#### Table\n\n- Import: `import { Table } from '@pages/orin/Table'` (also exports type `TableProps`)\n- Source: `packages/orin/src/table/table.tsx`; recipe: `tableRecipe` in `packages/orin/src/table/tableRecipe.ts`.\n- Tests: `packages/orin/src/table/table.test.tsx`.\n- What it renders: a keyboard-focusable scroll region named by the caption, holding a `<table>` with a mono column-label row. The first cell of each row is its row header.\n- Usage: in use. Consumers in apps: orin-dx: tool pages, the Caliper evidence pages.\n\n**Props**\n\n| Prop | Type | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `caption` | `string` | required | Names the scroll region and the table. |\n| `hideCaption` | `boolean` | `false` | Keeps the caption for assistive technology and does not draw it, when a heading above names the table. |\n| `columns` | `readonly string[]` | required | The column labels. Keep each to one short word where you can: a heading that repeats a tool's name across columns reads badly. Put the tool in a column instead (one row per tool). |\n| `rows` | `readonly (readonly ReactNode[])[]` | required | One array of cells per row. |\n| `groupSize` | `number` | none | Rows that belong together, such as a Caliper row and its RDT row: a heavier rule closes each group. |\n| `rowTones` | `readonly ('focus' \\\\| 'reference' \\\\| undefined)[]` | none | The role of each row by index, in the colours the charts use: `focus` is the subject in `text.measure`, `reference` is what it is held against in `text.muted`. |\n| `classes` | `{ root?, table?, caption?, head?, cell? }` (strings) | none | Appended per slot by `mergeSlots`. |\n| `...rest` | `ComponentPropsWithRef<'div'>` minus `children`, `className` | none | Spread onto the root `<div>`. |\n\n**Attributes emitted**: `data-recipe=\"table\"` on the root, `data-slot` on each part, `data-group-end` on every cell of the last row of a group, `data-tone` on every cell of a toned row.\n\n**Accessibility**:\n\n- The root is `role=\"region\"` with `aria-label` equal to the caption and `tabIndex={0}`, so a table wider than its column scrolls by keyboard.\n- Colour is never the only carrier: a toned row also names its tool in a cell, and the values are always written out.\n\n\"\"\"\nreplace_once(\"#### PageSection\\n\", table + \"#### PageSection\\n\")\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(text)\nprint('api reference updated')\nEOF","description":"Update the API reference for Lattice, ToolHero and Table"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"025ff3e1-60b5-499a-81a7-a97589d02a1f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwZsk2HUKgY8whYavUxY","requestRef":"0560dd89-e432-4703-8c7f-e900864da789","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a9997aa-09ba-4b98-9b08-9207d4a3fe5f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:53:19.376Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
