{"parentUuid":"dc902933-35d6-4c62-b997-bc3ced957d88","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZvyU1fPKCGKZJSjf9V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The API reference is updated. Now the evidence guide: its last section (\"First application\") describes charts that no longer exist, and it lacks the recipe we ended up with."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2765,"cache_read_input_tokens":720265,"output_tokens":2838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":843},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2838,"cache_read_input_tokens":720265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd37e2fa-875e-4f01-bd08-0c4a70c08193","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwZvy3DVKfGbQRRqmL65","requestRef":"09b0b522-66c7-49dc-8150-157f1254bdd4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b84365b0-4c7e-48cd-92c5-66b71d2009cd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:53:56.573Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"b84365b0-4c7e-48cd-92c5-66b71d2009cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZvyU1fPKCGKZJSjf9V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A1CEmJTLHfDZnNmAyftpoR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && cat > \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/evidoc.py\" <<'EOF'\npath = 'docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md'\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\nold_bullet = \"- Long tool documents should use the existing chapter rail from `DocumentPage`, with source notes beside the claims they support.\"\nnew_bullet = \"- Tool pages and their evidence pages are document pages: the chapter rail from `DocumentPage` names the sections, and source notes sit beside the claims they support.\"\nassert text.count(old_bullet) == 1\ntext = text.replace(old_bullet, new_bullet)\n\nmarker = \"## First application\"\nassert text.count(marker) == 1\nhead = text[: text.index(marker)]\n\ntail = \"\"\"## An evidence page\n\nThe Caliper pages that carry a comparison (how right the props are, how fast and light the run is) follow one recipe. It came out of repeated review, and each rule answers a mistake we made.\n\n1. **The claim is in the lede, in numbers.** One sentence with every finding the page proves, including where the subject falls short. No adjective stands in for a figure.\n2. **Who judges comes before the first chart.** A short section names the arbiter (TypeScript's checker) and that both tools are held to it by the same rules. The tool being compared against is a baseline, not the reference.\n3. **One idea per section, as a question.** The title asks it; the description picks up where the last section stopped (\"Start with the claim that matters most\", \"Rarely wrong is not enough if the rest is looser\"); one chart answers it. A page that crams every measure into one figure reads as noise.\n4. **Charts use `ComparisonBars` and the role colours.** `focus` is the subject, `reference` is what it is held against. Like units share one scale from zero. Scale each pair to its own longer bar only when the ratio is the story (time, memory), and write the ratio at the group's right.\n5. **Show the count with its share and its unit.** A count alone misleads: a prop used by 700 components counts 700 times, so one cause looks large. Give the share of what each tool lists, and say what is counted.\n6. **State each tool's scope.** If one tool is scored on every function it lists and the other only on components it reports, the page says so beside the figure. Real components are defined once, and the tool that supplies that list is not scored on it.\n7. **Pairs read as pairs.** A comparison table has one row per tool per subject, the tool in a column, single-word headings, rows toned by role (`rowTones`) and a heavier rule closing each pair (`groupSize`). Do not repeat a tool's name across column headings.\n8. **Examples are code with a consequence.** Use `TypeBoundaries`: the declaration where we have it, what each tool prints, then a sentence on what a reader of the docs sees. The page says once which examples come from a real library; headings carry the mistake, not its provenance. State plainly when the record keeps counts but not the props behind them.\n9. **Name where it falls short, and what is unknown.** Give the causes the record supports, with the counts. Say \"we have not established why\" where that is true. A zero is not a clean bill if the comparison cannot see a class of error.\n10. **One dated record feeds every page.** Figures come from `apps/orin-dx/src/data/caliperRecord.ts` (date, version, runner), never typed into a page, so the main page, the parity page and the measurement page cannot disagree. A page that quotes a figure from another run names that run.\n\n### Layout\n\n- An evidence page is a document page. The breadcrumb trail goes before the `DocumentPage` wrapper; the hero is its lead (`ToolPageHero` with a `title` and `art=\"none\"`, so the page names itself, shows no chips or actions and has the lattice alone); sections are `width=\"frame\"` with a small spacing wrapper because `PageSection` does not space children in that mode.\n- The rail numbers the sections, so each section's label is a word, matching its chapter label. Build the chapters from the same conditions that decide which sections exist.\n- Previous and next cards go in the `footer` slot, inside a `data-reading` frame, so they sit on the reading column.\n- Layers use role tokens, never literals or another component's token: `zIndex.rail` for the chapter list and `zIndex.trail` for the breadcrumb trail, one step above it so a menu opened from the trail covers the list.\n\n## First application\n\nThe Caliper parity page now answers three questions in order (is a type ever wrong, do the props each tool lists match the checker, does Caliper report the real components) with three shared-scale charts, a paired-row table, `TypeBoundaries` examples and a section on where Caliper falls short. The measurement page asks how much faster and how much lighter, with speed and memory charts, the Storybook session figures and the limits. Both read the November 9, 2026 weekly record. Callisto, Michi, Monokl and Wisp use the same source-note and code treatments, with numbered feature rows only where the copy is short enough to scan. Longer pages keep their card groups. The five-series sequence remains a proposal to test in both themes before updating the brand library source and generated semantic tokens together.\n\"\"\"\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(head + tail)\nprint('evidence guide updated')\nEOF\npython3 -I \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/evidoc.py\"; tail -5 docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md | head -3","description":"Rewrite the evidence guide's recipe, layout notes and first application","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2765,"cache_read_input_tokens":720265,"output_tokens":2838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":843},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2838,"cache_read_input_tokens":720265,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01A1CEmJTLHfDZnNmAyftpoR":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && cat > \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/evidoc.py\" <<'EOF'\npath = 'docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md'\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\nold_bullet = \"- Long tool documents should use the existing chapter rail from `DocumentPage`, with source notes beside the claims they support.\"\nnew_bullet = \"- Tool pages and their evidence pages are document pages: the chapter rail from `DocumentPage` names the sections, and source notes sit beside the claims they support.\"\nassert text.count(old_bullet) == 1\ntext = text.replace(old_bullet, new_bullet)\n\nmarker = \"## First application\"\nassert text.count(marker) == 1\nhead = text[: text.index(marker)]\n\ntail = \"\"\"## An evidence page\n\nThe Caliper pages that carry a comparison (how right the props are, how fast and light the run is) follow one recipe. It came out of repeated review, and each rule answers a mistake we made.\n\n1. **The claim is in the lede, in numbers.** One sentence with every finding the page proves, including where the subject falls short. No adjective stands in for a figure.\n2. **Who judges comes before the first chart.** A short section names the arbiter (TypeScript's checker) and that both tools are held to it by the same rules. The tool being compared against is a baseline, not the reference.\n3. **One idea per section, as a question.** The title asks it; the description picks up where the last section stopped (\"Start with the claim that matters most\", \"Rarely wrong is not enough if the rest is looser\"); one chart answers it. A page that crams every measure into one figure reads as noise.\n4. **Charts use `ComparisonBars` and the role colours.** `focus` is the subject, `reference` is what it is held against. Like units share one scale from zero. Scale each pair to its own longer bar only when the ratio is the story (time, memory), and write the ratio at the group's right.\n5. **Show the count with its share and its unit.** A count alone misleads: a prop used by 700 components counts 700 times, so one cause looks large. Give the share of what each tool lists, and say what is counted.\n6. **State each tool's scope.** If one tool is scored on every function it lists and the other only on components it reports, the page says so beside the figure. Real components are defined once, and the tool that supplies that list is not scored on it.\n7. **Pairs read as pairs.** A comparison table has one row per tool per subject, the tool in a column, single-word headings, rows toned by role (`rowTones`) and a heavier rule closing each pair (`groupSize`). Do not repeat a tool's name across column headings.\n8. **Examples are code with a consequence.** Use `TypeBoundaries`: the declaration where we have it, what each tool prints, then a sentence on what a reader of the docs sees. The page says once which examples come from a real library; headings carry the mistake, not its provenance. State plainly when the record keeps counts but not the props behind them.\n9. **Name where it falls short, and what is unknown.** Give the causes the record supports, with the counts. Say \"we have not established why\" where that is true. A zero is not a clean bill if the comparison cannot see a class of error.\n10. **One dated record feeds every page.** Figures come from `apps/orin-dx/src/data/caliperRecord.ts` (date, version, runner), never typed into a page, so the main page, the parity page and the measurement page cannot disagree. A page that quotes a figure from another run names that run.\n\n### Layout\n\n- An evidence page is a document page. The breadcrumb trail goes before the `DocumentPage` wrapper; the hero is its lead (`ToolPageHero` with a `title` and `art=\"none\"`, so the page names itself, shows no chips or actions and has the lattice alone); sections are `width=\"frame\"` with a small spacing wrapper because `PageSection` does not space children in that mode.\n- The rail numbers the sections, so each section's label is a word, matching its chapter label. Build the chapters from the same conditions that decide which sections exist.\n- Previous and next cards go in the `footer` slot, inside a `data-reading` frame, so they sit on the reading column.\n- Layers use role tokens, never literals or another component's token: `zIndex.rail` for the chapter list and `zIndex.trail` for the breadcrumb trail, one step above it so a menu opened from the trail covers the list.\n\n## First application\n\nThe Caliper parity page now answers three questions in order (is a type ever wrong, do the props each tool lists match the checker, does Caliper report the real components) with three shared-scale charts, a paired-row table, `TypeBoundaries` examples and a section on where Caliper falls short. The measurement page asks how much faster and how much lighter, with speed and memory charts, the Storybook session figures and the limits. Both read the November 9, 2026 weekly record. Callisto, Michi, Monokl and Wisp use the same source-note and code treatments, with numbered feature rows only where the copy is short enough to scan. Longer pages keep their card groups. The five-series sequence remains a proposal to test in both themes before updating the brand library source and generated semantic tokens together.\n\"\"\"\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(head + tail)\nprint('evidence guide updated')\nEOF\npython3 -I \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/evidoc.py\"; tail -5 docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md | head -3","description":"Rewrite the evidence guide's recipe, layout notes and first application","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd37e2fa-875e-4f01-bd08-0c4a70c08193","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgwZvy3DVKfGbQRRqmL65","requestRef":"09b0b522-66c7-49dc-8150-157f1254bdd4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4732ac01-24b0-419e-9d98-35b360c00ab8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:10.053Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
