{"parentUuid":"c9c60b55-44b5-4f1c-8149-deb1bea1967b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01DfZQUV1sNMP6KNdoHejrAE","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && rtk grep -n -i \\\"tool page\\\" docs/plans/page-layouts.md | head -12; ls apps/storybook/stories/orin | rtk grep -i -E \\\"table|toolhero|lattice\\\"; sed -n 1,40p apps/storybook/stories/orin/table.stories.tsx 2>/dev/null\",\"description\":\"Find tool-page layout rules and the existing Table story\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":14},"type":"attachment","uuid":"765762d5-8365-47e9-bb60-f4aef460d4f0","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:13.793Z","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"c9c60b55-44b5-4f1c-8149-deb1bea1967b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"59b8b9da-3745-4467-ad83-b44577dbb5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n28:1. **A page's first element sits `gap.block` (48px) under the nav**, on every page of both brands and at every width (changed 14 Oct 2026 from `gap.section`, 96px, which read as too much; phones now match). On Orin the art (the lit lattice with the ribbon or the mark) is placed from the same line, so it moves up with the text; techworx has no art and only its content moves. The one exception is a tool page, which has a breadcrumb row above its kicker: the trail sits `gap.items` (16px) under the nav and the kicker a `gap.paragraph` (24px) below it. The CV is locked and is not governed by this. Below the desktop frame width the art never leads the opener: a ribbon with its lattice sits behind the text, smaller and fainter and in the same place on every page (the landing page's), and a mark is a small 96px one in the flow.\n53:14. **The lattice and glow come in levels.** Landing 0.2 and 0.1; other pages 0.14 and 0.07; a tool page in its family colour at 0.26 and 0.18 in light and 0.3 and 0.26 on Case, to read like the social card. A tool page's lattice is always in its family colour; the haze comes only with the mark, and the art beside the text is the mark, the strands or nothing (a page under the tool's own, which has no star of its own). Hidden on phones; one fixed point on every page so it does not jump on navigation. The bottom-left footer echo is an option, not yet decided on techworx.\n55:15. **One star per page.** A page carries the brand mark or the ribbon, never both: the home page, Principles and tool pages lead with the ribbon over its lit lattice; the brand page leads with the mark and its glow. Strands elsewhere (card edges, the braid) are supporting and never compete with the star. The brand page shows both in the \"One star per page\" figures.\n67:- **Reading pages** (tool pages, Principles, brand pages, case studies, articles, About): content in the centre, between two equal rails. Left rail, columns 1–3: where you are (section labels, or the chapter list on documents). Content, columns 4–9: everything the reader reads or looks at, headings, text at the measure, images, figures, samples, tables and card rows. Right rail, columns 10–12: only facts and notes beside the content (owner decision, 2026-10-04: heroes and images never run into it). A tool page's own header spans 1–12; a document's hero also runs the page's width over the rails, with the chapters starting under it (rule 5 under \"Decided in review\").\n84:| Facts | Role, scope and stage on case studies; stage, family and source on tool pages | `FactsList`, `ToolFacts` |\n155:### Tool page (×9)\ncolour-tables.stories.tsx","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DfZQUV1sNMP6KNdoHejrAE"}]},"uuid":"3fe4a614-bcfd-472f-b8e7-69777746b484","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:17.104Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n28:1. **A page's first element sits `gap.block` (48px) under the nav**, on every page of both brands and at every width (changed 14 Oct 2026 from `gap.section`, 96px, which read as too much; phones now match). On Orin the art (the lit lattice with the ribbon or the mark) is placed from the same line, so it moves up with the text; techworx has no art and only its content moves. The one exception is a tool page, which has a breadcrumb row above its kicker: the trail sits `gap.items` (16px) under the nav and the kicker a `gap.paragraph` (24px) below it. The CV is locked and is not governed by this. Below the desktop frame width the art never leads the opener: a ribbon with its lattice sits behind the text, smaller and fainter and in the same place on every page (the landing page's), and a mark is a small 96px one in the flow.\n53:14. **The lattice and glow come in levels.** Landing 0.2 and 0.1; other pages 0.14 and 0.07; a tool page in its family colour at 0.26 and 0.18 in light and 0.3 and 0.26 on Case, to read like the social card. A tool page's lattice is always in its family colour; the haze comes only with the mark, and the art beside the text is the mark, the strands or nothing (a page under the tool's own, which has no star of its own). Hidden on phones; one fixed point on every page so it does not jump on navigation. The bottom-left footer echo is an option, not yet decided on techworx.\n55:15. **One star per page.** A page carries the brand mark or the ribbon, never both: the home page, Principles and tool pages lead with the ribbon over its lit lattice; the brand page leads with the mark and its glow. Strands elsewhere (card edges, the braid) are supporting and never compete with the star. The brand page shows both in the \"One star per page\" figures.\n67:- **Reading pages** (tool pages, Principles, brand pages, case studies, articles, About): content in the centre, between two equal rails. Left rail, columns 1–3: where you are (section labels, or the chapter list on documents). Content, columns 4–9: everything the reader reads or looks at, headings, text at the measure, images, figures, samples, tables and card rows. Right rail, columns 10–12: only facts and notes beside the content (owner decision, 2026-10-04: heroes and images never run into it). A tool page's own header spans 1–12; a document's hero also runs the page's width over the rails, with the chapters starting under it (rule 5 under \"Decided in review\").\n84:| Facts | Role, scope and stage on case studies; stage, family and source on tool pages | `FactsList`, `ToolFacts` |\n155:### Tool page (×9)\ncolour-tables.stories.tsx","classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"65819ac5-2332-4218-88d2-770ffb62bb15","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked