{"parentUuid":"85c8a9c5-6c2e-4e86-b5d3-d8b57ef0682a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwZyH6DhRzjyZatBNkkw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YUY952h7g29BqMadxN1gJy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && cat > \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/layoutdoc.py\" <<'EOF'\npath = 'docs/plans/page-layouts.md'\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\ndef replace_once(old, new):\n    global text\n    assert text.count(old) == 1, (text.count(old), old[:70])\n    text = text.replace(old, new)\n\nreplace_once(\n\"Left rail, columns 1–3: where you are (section labels, or the chapter list on documents).\",\n\"Left rail, columns 1–3: where you are (section labels, or the chapter list on documents and tool pages).\")\n\nreplace_once(\n\"- **Changes:** no split bands. Every section is a full-width, top-to-bottom block, so the page reads in one direction. Planned tools (firkin, pulse) stay short: hero, why, limits, what's next.\\n\",\n\"\"\"- **Changes:** no split bands. Every section is a full-width, top-to-bottom block, so the page reads in one direction. Planned tools (firkin, pulse) stay short: hero, why, limits, what's next.\n- **Chapters (added 11 Nov 2026):** a tool page is a document page. The chapter list names the sections in the left rail (every tool page has at least four, so the rail always shows), the breadcrumb trail sits above the document wrapper, the hero is the document's lead, sections are `frame` width on the reading column, and the previous and next cards sit in the `footer` slot inside a `data-reading` frame. The rail numbers the sections, so a section's label is a word, matching its chapter label.\n\n### Caliper evidence pages (×2)\n\n- **Job:** show that a claim on the Caliper page holds, with the method and the limits: how right the props are (parity), how fast and light the run is (measurement). The recipe is in `docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md`.\n- **Order:** hero (the page names itself, lattice alone, no chips) → who judges or how it was measured → one section per question, each with one chart → the counts as a paired-row table → examples (parity) or the Storybook session (measurement) → where it falls short → the method → what next.\n- **Changes:** a document page like a tool page. Figures come from one dated record, `apps/orin-dx/src/data/caliperRecord.ts`, so the pages cannot disagree with each other or with the Caliper page.\n\"\"\")\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(text)\nprint('layouts updated')\nEOF\npython3 -I \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/layoutdoc.py\"","description":"Update the page layouts doc for tool pages and the evidence pages","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":727390,"output_tokens":1365,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":375},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":727390,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YUY952h7g29BqMadxN1gJy":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/projects/pages && cat > \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/layoutdoc.py\" <<'EOF'\npath = 'docs/plans/page-layouts.md'\ntext = open(path, encoding='utf-8').read()\n\ndef replace_once(old, new):\n    global text\n    assert text.count(old) == 1, (text.count(old), old[:70])\n    text = text.replace(old, new)\n\nreplace_once(\n\"Left rail, columns 1–3: where you are (section labels, or the chapter list on documents).\",\n\"Left rail, columns 1–3: where you are (section labels, or the chapter list on documents and tool pages).\")\n\nreplace_once(\n\"- **Changes:** no split bands. Every section is a full-width, top-to-bottom block, so the page reads in one direction. Planned tools (firkin, pulse) stay short: hero, why, limits, what's next.\\n\",\n\"\"\"- **Changes:** no split bands. Every section is a full-width, top-to-bottom block, so the page reads in one direction. Planned tools (firkin, pulse) stay short: hero, why, limits, what's next.\n- **Chapters (added 11 Nov 2026):** a tool page is a document page. The chapter list names the sections in the left rail (every tool page has at least four, so the rail always shows), the breadcrumb trail sits above the document wrapper, the hero is the document's lead, sections are `frame` width on the reading column, and the previous and next cards sit in the `footer` slot inside a `data-reading` frame. The rail numbers the sections, so a section's label is a word, matching its chapter label.\n\n### Caliper evidence pages (×2)\n\n- **Job:** show that a claim on the Caliper page holds, with the method and the limits: how right the props are (parity), how fast and light the run is (measurement). The recipe is in `docs/plans/tool-evidence-language.md`.\n- **Order:** hero (the page names itself, lattice alone, no chips) → who judges or how it was measured → one section per question, each with one chart → the counts as a paired-row table → examples (parity) or the Storybook session (measurement) → where it falls short → the method → what next.\n- **Changes:** a document page like a tool page. Figures come from one dated record, `apps/orin-dx/src/data/caliperRecord.ts`, so the pages cannot disagree with each other or with the Caliper page.\n\"\"\")\nopen(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(text)\nprint('layouts updated')\nEOF\npython3 -I \"$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/layoutdoc.py\"","description":"Update the page l