rolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"c733b0c3-8902-4658-ace8-fa242c08abc5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"59b8b9da-3745-4467-ad83-b44577dbb5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014qGmX9xJjRQ53y5SL34mXy","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 9 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: plan-trails-before-branches\n3\tdescription: \"In caliper, plan feature-focused trails and assign branches to them on paper before creating any trail, branch or PR; open PRs only through the gh shim, then link at once\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: cd0b1cc5-b31e-40d5-8c38-bf89ad8b231e\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-02T15:13:41.499Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tPlan the work as feature-focused trails, with every planned branch assigned to a trail (and its base, and any stack position), and show the plan before creating anything. Don't rush into branches. A trail is one feature or semantic group; each branch/PR is a change under it. Don't create one trail per PR.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** on 2026-10-31/11-01 PRs went out first and trails were reorganised afterwards. Entire auto-created duplicate trails (#134), a change cannot be reparented once it belongs to a trail (409; `unlink` refuses to detach, the CLI has no reparent or delete), so #270 and #271 ended up in the wrong trails. The user said: \"plan trails first and assign branches to it first. Don't rush.\"\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:**\n16\t1. Write the plan first: trail title and acceptance criteria, then each branch (name, base, stacked or independent, files it touches, owner). Decide stack vs parallel by file overlap. Get a yes.\n17\t2. Create the trails (intent-only, `entire trail create --no-branch`), then branches, then open every PR in one batch so one Touch ID approval covers them.\n18\t3. Flow from another session (2026-11-02): merging happens in the Entire UI and the trail approval is the gate, so a PR Entire opens (authored as the user) is fine. Link-first works: create the trail intent-only, push branches, `entire trail link <n> --branch <b> --base main`, Entire opens the PR, then edit its title and body keeping the `entire-shadow-pr` marker (don't run `gh pr create`). Observed here: linking a STACKED branch (PR already open with a non-main base) made Entire open a second draft PR against main (#277, #278), so give stacked links the right `--base` before the PR exists, or link before opening a PR by hand. I replaced Entire-opened bodies earlier and the marker was not in them.\n19\t3b. The shim route: PRs opened directly are opened with `gh pr create` only: the global `gh` shim (~/.local/bin/gh) runs it as the orin-dx-pr-bot so a human can approve. It covers `pr create` only (edit/ready/comment run as the user), fails closed, needs Touch ID, and `~/.config/orin-dx` and the bot's app-support dirs are off limits (the global guard hook blocks commands that mention bot credentials, even in a history search). Subagents must not open PRs; the lead does, from a body file.\n20\t4. Link each branch to its planned trail immediately after `gh pr create` (`entire trail link <n> --branch <b>`); it reuses the PR and makes no duplicate. Verify with `entire trail show <n> --json`.\n21\t5. Before any push run the whole CI set, not a subset of crates: `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked`, `just lint doc-check typos machete`, TS package tests if packages/ changed (a missed CLI-crate literal broke #271 once).\n22\t\n23\tSee [[stacked-pr-retargeting]] and [[sandbox-git-and-gh]].\n24\t"}]},"uuid":"0184763f-54ee-48c5-9bfb-02a968d632f6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:54:54.821Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/plan-trails-before-branches.md","content":"---\nname: plan-trails-before-branches\ndescription: \"In caliper, plan feature-focused trails and assign branches to them on paper before creating any trail, branch or PR; open PRs only through the gh shim, then link at once\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: cd0b1cc5-b31e-40d5-8c38-bf89ad8b231e\n  modified: 2026-11-02T15:13:41.499Z\n---\n\nPlan the work as feature-focused trails, with every planned branch assigned to a trail (and its base, and any stack position), and show the plan before creating anything. Don't rush into branches. A trail is one feature or semantic group; each branch/PR is a change under it. Don't create one trail per PR.\n\n**Why:** on 2026-10-31/11-01 PRs went out first and trails were reorganised afterwards. Entire auto-created duplicate trails (#134), a change cannot be reparented once it belongs to a trail (409; `unlink` refuses to detach, the CLI has no reparent or delete), so #270 and #271 ended up in the wrong trails. The user said: \"plan trails first and assign branches to it first. Don't rush.\"\n\n**How to apply:**\n1. Write the plan first: trail title and acceptance criteria, then each branch (name, base, stacked or independent, files it touches, owner). Decide stack vs parallel by file overlap. Get a yes.\n2. Create the trails (intent-only, `entire trail create --no-branch`), then branches, then open every PR in one batch so one Touch ID approval covers them.\n3. Flow from another session (2026-11-02): merging happens in the Entire UI and the trail approval is the gate, so a PR Entire opens (authored as the user) is fine. Link-first works: create the trail intent-only, push branches, `entire trail link <n> --branch <b> --base main`, Entire opens the PR, then edit its title and body keeping the `entire-shadow-pr` marker (don't run `gh pr create`). Observed here: linking a STACKED branch (PR already open with a non-main base) made Entire open a second draft PR against main (#277, #278), so give stacked links the right `--base` before the PR exists, or link before opening a PR by hand. I replaced Entire-opened bodies earlier and the marker was not in them.\n3b. The shim route: PRs opened directly are opened with `gh pr create` only: the global `gh` shim (~/.local/bin/gh) runs it as the orin-dx-pr-bot so a human can approve. It covers `pr create` only (edit/ready/comment run as the user), fails closed, needs Touch ID, and `~/.config/orin-dx` and the bot's app-support dirs are off limits (the global guard hook blocks commands that mention bot credentials, even in a history search). Subagents must not open PRs; the lead does, from a body file.\n4. Link each branch to its planned trail immediately after `gh pr create` (`entire trail link <n> --branch <b>`); it reuses the PR and makes no duplicate. Verify with `entire trail show <n> --json`.\n5. Before any push run the whole CI set, not a subset of crates: `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked`, `just lint doc-check typos machete`, TS package tests if packages/ changed (a missed CLI-crate literal broke #271 once).\n\nSee [[stacked-pr-retargeting]] and [[sandbox-git-and-gh]].\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c733b0c3-8902-4658-ace8-fa242c08abc5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
