{"parentUuid":"1a56c764-ff49-4c09-8cd5-c1057786cc58","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwa344VvD4kKZANQhdDw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0144XwnpYv8fMnJbBUfJEAFJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/4c72440d/tmp/weekly/weekly/weekly.json'))\nprint('| corpus | shared | less | wrong | any/err | agree | wrong% | RDT wrong% |')\nfor c,v in d['corpora'].items():\n    o=v['oracle']; t=o['tools']; C=t['caliper']; R=t['rdt']\n    ver=C['verdicts']\n    print(c, o['shared_props'], ver.get('less precise',0), ver.get('wrong',0), ver.get('checker any/error',0), round(o['agree']*100,1) if o['agree']<=1 else o['agree'], o['wrong'], round(R['wrong_listed']*100,3))\nEOF\ncd /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper && /usr/bin/git show origin/main:docs/rdt-differences.md | grep -n -i -E \"until it merges|comparator fix|after the fix|fixed in the comparator|2026-11-06|1\\.09%|22 wrong\" | head -14; /usr/bin/git show origin/main:docs/rdt-differences.md | sed -n 18,34p","description":"Compute the November 9 oracle table and find stale lines in rdt-differences"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6469,"cache_read_input_tokens":734296,"output_tokens":2225,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1725},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2225,"cache_read_input_tokens":734296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6469},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0144XwnpYv8fMnJbBUfJEAFJ":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/4c72440d/tmp/weekly/weekly/weekly.json'))\nprint('| corpus | shared | less | wrong | any/err | agree | wrong% | RDT wrong% |')\nfor c,v in d['corpora'].items():\n    o=v['oracle']; t=o['tools']; C=t['caliper']; R=t['rdt']\n    ver=C['verdicts']\n    print(c, o['shared_props'], ver.get('less precise',0), ver.get('wrong',0), ver.get('checker any/error',0), round(o['agree']*100,1) if o['agree']<=1 else o['agree'], o['wrong'], round(R['wrong_listed']*100,3))\nEOF\ncd /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper && /usr/bin/git show origin/main:docs/rdt-differences.md | grep -n -i -E \"until it merges|comparator fix|after the fix|fixed in the comparator|2026-11-06|1\\.09%|22 wrong\" | head -14; /usr/bin/git show origin/main:docs/rdt-differences.md | sed -n 18,34p","description":"Compute the November 9 oracle table and find stale lines in rdt-differences"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4cb06775-bdce-4e7c-8977-4287fcce47af","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgwa33eT21mkrqeAhRDoc","requestRef":"e8dc94d7-3e3f-4a74-9528-954b9df13480","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7c87ab1a-bf5d-46a1-a5ce-13cfd3ea3664","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:55:26.858Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"7c87ab1a-bf5d-46a1-a5ce-13cfd3ea3664","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"59b8b9da-3745-4467-ad83-b44577dbb5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0144XwnpYv8fMnJbBUfJEAFJ","type":"tool_result","content":"| corpus | shared | less | wrong | any/err | agree | wrong% | RDT wrong% |\nmantine 20104 1281 0 8 93.6 0.0 0.045\nchakra 486832 19 1 0 100.0 2.0540966904394123e-06 0.006\nshadcn 13863 696 0 60 94.5 0.0 0.547\nantd 3426 195 1 1 94.2 0.0002918855808523059 1.046\nspectrum 2023 102 0 208 84.7 0.0 5.024\n21:Measured 2026-11-06 on `main` at `c5fbb33e`, the pinned corpora, `scripts/weekly.py --oracle`:\n29:| spectrum |        2,023 |          100 |    22 |               208 |  83.7% |   1.09% |                  5.02% |\n37:### 1. Index signatures (comparator artifact, fixed in the comparator fix)\n53:**Measured.** 28 of the 31 `wrong` are this, and all 28 are false. After the comparator fix an index signature is compared as an index signature and these props are identical or spelled. Until it merges, spectrum's 22 wrong (1.09%) are above the gate for this reason alone.\n55:**Accounted.** Documented here; the comparator fix removes it.\n57:### 2. `readonly` (comparator artifact, fixed in the comparator fix)\n72:**Measured.** 22 props across the corpora score `less precise` for this. After the fix the comparator looks through `readonly`.\n74:**Accounted.** Documented here; the comparator fix removes it. It moves `less precise` into `identical`, so it moves `agree` and not `wrong`.\n76:### 3. `'a' | string` against `string & {}` (comparator artifact, fixed in the comparator fix)\n92:**Measured.** About 166 props score `less precise` for this. After the fix the comparator reads `string` beside the checker's `string & {}` as the same type.\n94:**Accounted.** Documented here; the comparator fix removes it.\n\n`agree` is identical plus spelled over the shared props. It is the looser number: `less precise` hides real imprecision and, as the classes below show, some real errors. `wrong` is the number that matters, and the gate: the weekly issue opens above 0.1% of the judged props (`docs/measurement.md`, \"The headline\"). `wrong` both over-triggers (a comparator artifact, classes 1 to 3) and under-triggers (silent wrong answers scored `less precise`, class 5), so read it with this page.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-06 on `main` at `c5fbb33e`, the pinned corpora, `scripts/weekly.py --oracle`:\n\n| Corpus   | Shared props | Less precise | Wrong | Checker any/error |  agree |   wrong | RDT wrong (same props) |\n| -------- | -----------: | -----------: | ----: | ----------------: | -----: | ------: | ---------------------: |\n| mantine  |       20,104 |        1,828 |     0 |                 8 |  90.9% |       0 |                  0.04% |\n| chakra   |      486,832 |           22 |     1 |                 0 | 100.0% | 0.0002% |                 0.006% |\n| shadcn   |       13,863 |          738 |     8 |                60 |  94.2% |  0.058% |                  0.59% |\n| antd     |        3,426 |          205 |     0 |                 1 |  94.0% |       0 |                  1.05% |\n| spectrum |        2,023 |          100 |    22 |               208 |  83.7% |   1.09% |                  5.02% |\n\nThe last column is `oracle.tools.rdt.wrong_listed`: the share of the props RDT lists that the checker contradicts. It is over every function the checker takes for a component, as the record was until `universe_version` 2 (2026-11-10); a later record has it over candidate components only (`oracle.tools`) and over every function in `oracle.tools_all_functions`, and its spectrum row has more shared props, because default exports are named (`docs/measurement.md`). react-docgen throws on 51 of 295 antd files and 265 of 1,240 shadcn files (17% and 21%) and so omits their props.\n\nThe 31 wrong verdicts are 28 index-signature artifacts (class 1), 2 silent call-signature errors (class 4) and 1 narrower type from a factory (class 6). The 3,201 shared props that are not agree are 2,893 less precise, 31 wrong and 277 checker any/error.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"88905837-639c-4d02-8955-6ac5e84602b4","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:55:27.139Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"| corpus | shared | less | wrong | any/err | agree | wrong% | RDT wrong% |\nmantine 20104 1281 0 8 93.6 0.0 0.045\nchakra 486832 19 1 0 100.0 2.0540966904394123e-06 0.006\nshadcn 13863 696 0 60 94.5 0.0 0.547\nantd 3426 195 1 1 94.2 0.0002918855808523059 1.046\nspectrum 2023 102 0 208 84.7 0.0 5.024\n21:Measured 2026-11-06 on `main` at `c5fbb33e`, the pinned corpora, `scripts/weekly.py --oracle`:\n29:| spectrum |        2,023 |          100 |    22 |               208 |  83.7% |   1.09% |                  5.02% |\n37:### 1. Index signatures (comparator artifact, fixed in the comparator fix)\n53:**Measured.** 28 of the 31 `wrong` are this, and all 28 are false. After the comparator fix an index signature is compared as an index signature and these props are identical or spelled. Until it merges, spectrum's 22 wrong (1.09%) are above the gate for this reason alone.\n55:**Accounted.** Documented here; the comparator fix removes it.\n57:### 2. `readonly` (comparator artifact, fixed in the comparator fix)\n72:**Measured.** 22 props across the corpora score `less precise` for this. After the fix the comparator looks through `readonly`.\n74:**Accounted.** Documented here; the comparator fix removes it. It moves `less precise` into `identical`, so it moves `agree` and not `wrong`.\n76:### 3. `'a' | string` against `string & {}` (comparator artifact, fixed in the comparator fix)\n92:**Measured.** About 166 props score `less precise` for this. After the fix the comparator reads `string` beside the checker's `string & {}` as the same type.\n94:**Accounted.** Documented here; the comparator fix removes it.\n\n`agree` is identical plus spelled over the shared props. It is the looser number: `less precise` hides real imprecision and, as