{"parentUuid":"d58d3e20-cd82-4d36-b80b-d6dde66b0fac","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"59b8b9da-3745-4467-ad83-b44577dbb5ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dy9v5cy6J9nvEnKqgkaZb4","type":"tool_result","content":"[{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-09T14:42:10Z\",\"databaseId\":42637254796,\"event\":\"schedule\",\"headSha\":\"5be99000dd43d13d974438d9701414db8a902ad0\"},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-02T16:11:24Z\",\"databaseId\":41479003541,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"53970b80a5171441b2715a53c58ba819462a587f\"},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-02T14:13:59Z\",\"databaseId\":41459968910,\"event\":\"schedule\",\"headSha\":\"e2064d2362825ba93d6fec92cd4773ee72481a52\"},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-31T02:21:54Z\",\"databaseId\":41159666463,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"240a61c985479d3446f987189f4e642c11f5e354\"}]\n103:**What changed on 2026-11-10 (`oracle.universe_version` 2).** Until then the universe counted every such function, and a default export was keyed `default`. On the 2026-11-09 weekly, whole-universe agreement on react-spectrum read Caliper 30.7% against RDT 42.5% of 5,582 props, which read as Caliper being less complete. It was two artifacts, both measured on the saved dump of that run (`apps/oracle/tests/spectrum-universe.test.ts`):\n110:`oracle.shared_props`, `agree` and `wrong` keep their meaning, over the props both tools list. Naming default exports lets Caliper's `Foo` meet the checker's `Foo`, so a corpus with default-exported components, spectrum above all, has more shared props than before (2,023 in the record of 2026-11-06); no other change reaches them. A record without `universe_version` is version 1: its `tools` count every function, with a default export named `default`. A record of version 2 keeps the scores over every function, default exports named, in `oracle.tools_all_functions`, and counts what was left out in `oracle.universe_excluded` (functions and props, by rule). The summary prints both, and the weekly does not read a rise in wrong types, or any other number of the oracle, against a record of another version.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a433611e-bf8e-4788-b20c-5995bad112cd","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:55:34.977Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"[{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-09T14:42:10Z\",\"databaseId\":42637254796,\"event\":\"schedule\",\"headSha\":\"5be99000dd43d13d974438d9701414db8a902ad0\"},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-02T16:11:24Z\",\"databaseId\":41479003541,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"53970b80a5171441b2715a53c58ba819462a587f\"},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-02T14:13:59Z\",\"databaseId\":41459968910,\"event\":\"schedule\",\"headSha\":\"e2064d2362825ba93d6fec92cd4773ee72481a52\"},{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-31T02:21:54Z\",\"databaseId\":41159666463,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"240a61c985479d3446f987189f4e642c11f5e354\"}]\n103:**What changed on 2026-11-10 (`oracle.universe_version` 2).** Until then the universe counted every such function, and a default export was keyed `default`. On the 2026-11-09 weekly, whole-universe agreement on react-spectrum read Caliper 30.7% against RDT 42.5% of 5,582 props, which read as Caliper being less complete. It was two artifacts, both measured on the saved dump of that run (`apps/oracle/tests/spectrum-universe.test.ts`):\n110:`oracle.shared_props`, `agree` and `wrong` keep their meaning, over the props both tools list. Naming default exports lets Caliper's `Foo` meet the checker's `Foo`, so a corpus with default-exported components, spectrum above all, has more shared props than before (2,023 in the record of 2026-11-06); no other change reaches them. A record without `universe_version` is version 1: its `tools` count every function, with a default export named `default`. A record of version 2 keeps the scores over every function, default exports named, in `oracle.tools_all_functions`, and counts what was left out in `oracle.universe_excluded` (functions and props, by rule). The summary prints both, and the weekly does not read a rise in wrong types, or any other number of the oracle, against a record of another version.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"acf93fe5-b9e4-418b-bb06-afceabd1f847","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d58d3e20-cd82-4d36-b80b-d6dde66b0fac","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"main","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
