{"parentUuid":"c803b30b-acdc-4e81-ac0f-c647eed29744","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwa6njNcjJSD5GbDxDoj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The worktree is at the latest `main`. Applying the edits to the four Caliper docs with exact-match checks, so nothing changes if a passage has moved."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":754910,"output_tokens":8151,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4429},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8151,"cache_read_input_tokens":754910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ebf34a97-4419-4665-b40f-5faf6d89c12c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgwa6nKpaepLfj1brJGtQ","requestRef":"a1902f98-3a6c-43cf-af6a-ff334a08e1ad","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b14e10cc-095f-4cb1-a56a-f34c66cb0c51","timestamp":"2026-11-11T17:56:29.564Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/docs-align-weekly-2026-11-09","sessionId":"4c72440d-a6e2-4bf8-9c73-6f5da1acdec2","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"worktree-docs-align-weekly-2026-11-09","slug":"frolicking-percolating-waffle"}
{"parentUuid":"b14e10cc-095f-4cb1-a56a-f34c66cb0c51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwa6njNcjJSD5GbDxDoj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012dad5x5bnPJ1jETCXUsZRf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\ndef load(p): return open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef save(p, t): open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(t)\ndef once(text, old, new):\n    assert text.count(old) == 1, (text.count(old), old[:80])\n    return text.replace(old, new)\n\n# ---------- STATUS.md\np = 'docs/STATUS.md'\nt = load(p)\nt = once(t,\n \"on the props both list, the checker contradicts Caliper on 0 to 1.09% and RDT on 0.006 to 5.02%, `docs/rdt-differences.md`, 2026-11-06)\",\n \"on the props each tool lists, the checker contradicts 2 of Caliper's and 289 of RDT's across the five corpora, `docs/rdt-differences.md`, 2026-11-09; RDT's count is over every function it lists, which can include props of functions that are not components)\")\nlines = t.split('\\n')\nidx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"- **Speed** on five pinned public corpora\")]\nassert len(idx) == 1\nlines[idx[0]] = (\"- **Speed and memory** on five pinned public corpora (the weekly record of 2026-11-09, Caliper 0.10.0, a CI runner; `docs/measurement.md`): \"\n \"156 to 903 ms wall time and 179 to 451 MiB peak RSS, 16 to 66 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` (median 22) and 2.5 to 5.8 times less memory (median 4.0) on the same files. \"\n \"Caliper's figure is the median of five runs and RDT's one run, and a shared runner moves by 10% or more, so read the ratios. The laptop run of 2026-10-22 (`docs/performance.md`) read 17 to 39 times faster. \"\n \"No pull-request gate enforces it: a weekly workflow records speed, memory and recall against RDT and react-docgen and opens an issue on a worsening, and `just bench` compares a branch with `main` locally (`docs/measurement.md`).\")\nsave(p, '\\n'.join(lines))\n\n# ---------- measurement.md\np = 'docs/measurement.md'\nt = load(p)\nt = once(t,\n \"Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum read in that run: 90.9%, 100.0% and 83.7% agree, with 0, 1 and 22 wrong. Of Spectrum's 22, the comparator's index-signature artifact accounts for all (`docs/rdt-differences.md`), so that gate firing is false until the comparator is corrected.\",\n \"Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum read in that run: 90.9%, 100.0% and 83.7% agree, with 0, 1 and 22 wrong; all 22 of Spectrum's were the comparator's index-signature artifact (`docs/rdt-differences.md`). The comparator was corrected before the run of 2026-11-09, which reads 0 wrong on Spectrum and 0, 1, 0 and 1 on Mantine, Chakra, shadcn and antd (\\\"Results, 2026-11-09\\\" below).\")\n\nnew_section = \"\"\"## Results, 2026-11-09\n\nThe weekly record of run 42637254796 (`main` at `5be99000`, Caliper 0.10.0, a GitHub-hosted runner), made before `oracle.universe_version` 2. Time and peak RSS are one whole process each, Node start included: Caliper's is the median of five runs and RDT's one run, and a shared runner moves by 10% or more, so read the ratios and not the milliseconds.\n\n| Corpus   | Caliper          | RDT                | Faster | Less memory |\n| -------- | ---------------- | ------------------ | -----: | ----------: |\n| mantine  | 286 ms, 219 MiB  | 4.7 s, 539 MiB     |    16× |        2.5× |\n| chakra   | 903 ms, 451 MiB  | 59.3 s, 2,084 MiB  |    66× |        4.6× |\n| shadcn   | 629 ms, 353 MiB  | 10.2 s, 1,400 MiB  |    16× |        4.0× |\n| antd     | 156 ms, 179 MiB  | 6.1 s, 1,038 MiB   |    39× |        5.8× |\n| spectrum | 274 ms, 233 MiB  | 6.0 s, 816 MiB     |    22× |        3.5× |\n\nThe median is 22 times faster and 4.0 times less memory. Types, over the props each tool lists, judged by the checker (`oracle.tools`, version 1):\n\n| Corpus   | Listed (Caliper / RDT) | Agree         | Wrong    | Less precise                |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ------------- | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| mantine  | 20,104 / 20,117        | 93.6% / 97.1% | 0 / 9    | 1,281 (6.4%) / 576 (2.9%)   |\n| chakra   | 486,832 / 521,632      | 100.0% / 96.8% | 1 / 30  | 19 (<0.01%) / 16,642 (3.2%) |\n| shadcn   | 13,863 / 13,896        | 94.5% / 88.1% | 0 / 76   | 696 (5.0%) / 1,519 (10.9%)  |\n| antd     | 3,426 / 3,442          | 94.2% / 93.8% | 1 / 36   | 195 (5.7%) / 178 (5.2%)     |\n| spectrum | 2,023 / 2,747          | 84.7% / 86.3% | 0 / 138  | 102 (5.0%) / 52 (1.9%)      |\n\nComponents Caliper reports, of RDT's reference (its entries with props, less non-components and repeats, `reference_version` 2): mantine 328 of 368 (89.1%), chakra 614 of 664 (92.5%), shadcn 1,527 of 1,573 (97.1%), antd 188 of 202 (93.1%), spectrum 998 of 1,023 (97.6%). Of the own props RDT lists on those components, Caliper also lists 99.3% to 100%.\n\nHow to read these:\n\n- **A count is of (component, prop) pairs.** A prop declared once and used by 700 components counts 700 times, so one cause can look large. Chakra's 16,642 less precise props for RDT against Caliper's 19 is 3.2% against under 0.01% of what each lists. Read the shares as well as the counts.\n- **The shares are mixed.** Caliper leaves a higher share of props less precise than RDT on mantine (6.4% against 2.9%), antd (5.7% against 5.2%) and spectrum (5.0% against 1.9%), and a lower share on chakra and shadcn (5.0% against 10.9%). Less precise does not contradict the checker: it is a name left unexpanded, or a `Partial` or `Omit` through an alias (`docs/rdt-differences.md`, classes 5 and 7).\n- **Version 1 scopes the two tools differently.** RDT's figures are over every function the checker takes for a component that RDT lists, including hooks and helpers that are not components. Caliper's are over the components it reports. RDT's wrong and less precise counts can therefore run high. A record of version 2 scores both over candidate components (see \"What changed on 2026-11-10\" above).\n- **RDT's wrong count is also a floor.** A truncated type of RDT's is scored less precise and never wrong (`docs/rdt-differences.md`, class 8).\n- **The record keeps counts, not the props behind them.** The weekly cannot yet say which props make up a count, so an example of a wrong type comes from a reproduction and not from the record.\n\n\"\"\"\nt = once(t, \"## Results, 2026-10-23\\n\\nMeasured with the parity script this replaces:\",\n new_section + \"## Results, 2026-10-23\\n\\nSuperseded for speed and memory by the results of 2026-11-09 above, and kept as the 0.4.0 baseline. The column of non-React props reported is recall against RDT, which is information and not a measure of correctness. Measured with the parity script this replaces:\")\nsave(p, t)\n\n# ---------- rdt-differences.md\np = 'docs/rdt-differences.md'\nt = load(p)\nt = once(t,\n \"Until it merges, spectrum's 22 wrong (1.09%) are above the gate for this reason alone.\",\n \"Before the fix, spectrum's 22 wrong (1.09%) were above the gate for this reason alone; the record of 2026-11-09 reads 0.\")\nt = once(t,\n \"The 3,201 shared props that are not agree are 2,893 less precise, 31 wrong and 277 checker any/error.\",\n \"\"\"The 3,201 shared props that are not agree are 2,893 less precise, 31 wrong and 277 checker any/error.\n\nMeasured again on 2026-11-09 (run 42637254796, `main` at `5be99000`, after the comparator fix, `oracle.universe_version` 1):\n\n| Corpus   | Shared props | Less precise | Wrong | Checker any/error | agree  | wrong   | RDT wrong (same props) |\n| -------- | -----------: | -----------: | ----: | ----------------: | -----: | ------: | ---------------------: |\n| mantine  |       20,104 |        1,281 |     0 |                 8 |  93.6% |       0 |            0.04% (9)   |\n| chakra   |      486,832 |           19 |     1 |                 0 | 100.0% | 0.0002% |           0.006% (30)  |\n| shadcn   |       13,863 |          696 |     0 |                60 |  94.5% |       0 |            0.55% (76)  |\n| antd     |        3,426 |          195 |     1 |                 1 |  94.2% |   0.03% |            1.05% (36)  |\n| spectrum |        2,023 |          102 |     0 |               208 |  84.7% |       0 |           5.02% (138)  |\n\nThe fix cleared the index-signature artifacts (spectrum 22 wrong to 0, shadcn 8 to 0) and the `readonly` and `string & {}` classes (mantine's less precise props fell from 1,828 to 1,281). The 2 wrong that remain (one on chakra, one on antd) are not classified yet. The counts are (component, prop) pairs and RDT's cover every function it lists, as above, so read them with the shares in `docs/measurement.md`, \"Results, 2026-11-09\".\"\"\")\nsave(p, t)\nprint('edited')\nEOF\n/usr/bin/git diff --stat","description":"Apply the Caliper doc edits with exact-match assertions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":754910,"output_tokens":8151,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4429},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8151,"cache_read_input_tokens":754910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012dad5x5bnPJ1jETCXUsZRf":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\ndef load(p): return open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef save(p, t): open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(t)\ndef once(text, old, new):\n    assert text.count(old) == 1, (text.count(old), old[:80])\n    return text.replace(old, new)\n\n# ---------- STATUS.md\np = 'docs/